From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:58:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Sliders follow the mouse wheel only while Ctrl is held

Scrolling an options page could change a value whenever the cursor crossed a
slider. Without Ctrl the wheel now scrolls the area the slider sits in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
---
 src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/UI/Controls/HSliderBar.cs | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/UI/Controls/HSliderBar.cs b/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/UI/Controls/HSliderBar.cs
index 9f3d3841b..cb68b7e64 100644
--- a/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/UI/Controls/HSliderBar.cs
+++ b/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/UI/Controls/HSliderBar.cs
@@ -252,6 +252,17 @@ namespace ClassicUO.Game.UI.Controls
 
         protected override void OnMouseWheel(MouseEventType delta)
         {
+            // The wheel drives the slider only while Ctrl is held, so that scrolling a
+            // gump can't change a value by accident when the cursor crosses a slider.
+            // Without the modifier the event bubbles up, letting the ScrollArea below
+            // keep scrolling instead of swallowing it here.
+            if (!Keyboard.Ctrl)
+            {
+                base.OnMouseWheel(delta);
+
+                return;
+            }
+
             switch (delta)
             {
                 case MouseEventType.WheelScrollUp:
